<name>CVT</name>
<ttl id="1001Y_S000S_744HD_T007Y" variety="T007Y">
<name>CVT System [Super CVT-i] (K112/K112F)</name>
<para id="RM000001YAN00AX" category="D" type-id="304JI" name-id="3225K-00" from="200612">
<name>Freeze Frame Data</name>
<subpara id="RM000001YAN00AX_z0" proc-id="RM0550J___000047100000">
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<step1>
<ptxt>Check Freeze Frame Data</ptxt>
<step2>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), following the screen display, select the DTC recording freeze frame data (F displayed) from the [DTC Check] screen.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The engine condition (ECU data) at the time the DTC was detected and before and after detection (before: 1.5 seconds, after: 0.5 seconds) can be checked at 0.5-second intervals (time-series freeze frame data). However, if multiple DTCs are output, this applies only to the first DTC output. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005D5020X"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Check that the malfunction symptoms from the customer problem analysis are consistent with the Diagnostic Trouble Code Chart.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>After repair, perform a confirmation test referring to the driving conditions confirmed above.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
